Dear Mr Hamilton,

Further to our telephone call, I attach a draft Defence in the claim brought =
by Timothy Hamilton against Denise Parks (Claim No. K5DP8330).

I can confirm that the court (County Court at Cambridge) has listed the heari=
ng for 22 October 2021. Please confirm that you are able to attend.

Thank you for sending the documents. On a first review the case is well docum=
ented, although a few exhibits are still missing.

The draft is attached in Word format with tracked changes. Please send me you=
r comments by 31 May 2021, as the deadline for filing the response is fixed b=
y the court rules and cannot be extended without an application.

What we still need from you: confirmation of Timothy Hamilton's address (9 Mi=
ll Road, Birmingham B3 9YX), a copy of the payment slip for the deposit to ou=
r client account, and scans of your correspondence for the last two years.

The deposit towards court fees of =C2=A33,989.00 should reach our account GB3=
6SRLG60675069825656 no later than the day before the hearing.

You can upload documents and photographs through our secure client portal: ht=
tps://millstone.example.net/client/424377. Please do not send documents conta=
ining sensitive data by ordinary email.

Our witness, Gregory Murray, has been told that the court may require attenda=
nce; if his contact details (tel. 0121 496 0087) change, please let us know.

On strategy, I suggest we first seek the dismissal of the claim and, in the a=
lternative, ask the court to allow payment by instalments under CPR Part 40.

Please call me on +44 114 496 0850 or write to zfisher@example.org if you hav=
e any questions.

I am copying my colleague Jeffrey Holland so that he can follow the file whil=
e I am out of the office.

Kind regards,

